+en-GB:
+  STR_OPENXCOM: "OpenXcom 3D"
+  STR_FIRST_PERSON: "3D VIEW"
+  STR_FIRST_PERSON_TAB: "3D VIEW"
+  STR_FPS_SETTINGS: "Settings"
+  STR_FPS_CONTROLS: "Controls"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_3D: "3D"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_ISO: "ISO"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_HUD: "HUD"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_END_TURN: "END"
+  STR_FPS_ENEMY_SPOTTED: "ENEMY SPOTTED!"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_INVENTORY: "INV"
+  STR_FPS_MOUSE_SENSITIVITY: "Mouse sensitivity"
+  STR_FPS_MOUSE_SENSITIVITY_DESC: "How fast the view turns with the mouse (1-20). Left click raises, right click lowers."
+  STR_FPS_INVERT_MOUSE: "Invert mouse"
+  STR_FPS_INVERT_MOUSE_DESC: "Moving the mouse forward looks down instead of up."
+  STR_FPS_FIELD_OF_VIEW: "Field of view"
+  STR_FPS_FIELD_OF_VIEW_DESC: "Horizontal field of view of the 3D view in degrees (50-110). Left click raises, right click lowers."
+  STR_FPS_WALK_SPEED: "Walking speed"
+  STR_FPS_WALK_SPEED_DESC: "How fast the soldier walks in the 3D view, in tiles per second (1-8). Every tile entered still costs its normal time units."
+  STR_FPS_SMOOTH_LIGHTING: "Smooth lighting"
+  STR_FPS_SMOOTH_LIGHTING_DESC: "Blend the battlescape's light (sun, flares, fires, personal lights) smoothly between tiles instead of tile by tile."
+  STR_FPS_DOOM_MODE: "Doom mode (debug)"
+  STR_FPS_DOOM_MODE_DESC: "Cheat: the selected soldier never runs out of time units, energy or ammo. For testing and fun."
+  STR_FPS_DOOM: "DOOM MODE"
+  STR_FPS_KNEELING: "KNEELING"
+  STR_FPS_TU: "TU"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_SNAP: "SNAP"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_AIMED: "AIMED"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_AUTO: "AUTO"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_THROW: "THROW"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_LAUNCH: "LAUNCH"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_MELEE: "MELEE"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_PANIC: "PSI PANIC"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_MIND_CONTROL: "MIND CONTROL"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_USE: "USE"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_PRIME: "PRIME"
+  STR_FPS_PARTICLES: "Particles"
+  STR_FPS_PARTICLES_DESC: "0: none. 1: effects (muzzle flashes, impacts, explosions, fire, smoke). 2: everything, plus dust, fireflies, bubbles and weather."
+  STR_FPS_PIXEL_SIZE: "Pixel size"
+  STR_FPS_PIXEL_SIZE_DESC: "1: full detail. 2 or 3: chunkier pixels, much faster on big screens or slow machines."
+  STR_FPS_SOLDIER_PREVIEW: "SOLDIER CAMERA PREVIEW"
+  STR_FPS_SOLDIER_PREVIEW_DESC: "Hovering a soldier's button on the top bar shows a card with name, stats and weapon. With this on, the card also shows that soldier's helmet camera: what they are looking at, live."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_OPEN_DOOR: "Open door"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_OPEN_DOOR_DESC: "Opens the door in front of the soldier without walking through it (costs TU, like right-clicking it on the map)."
+  STR_FPS_WOUNDS: "WOUNDS {0}"
+  STR_FPS_HEAD_BOB: "Head bob"
+  STR_FPS_HEAD_BOB_DESC: "The view bobs gently with the soldier's steps. Turn it off if it makes you queasy."
+  STR_FPS_SHADOWS: "Shadows"
+  STR_FPS_SHADOWS_DESC: "Ray-traced shadows: from the sun by day, from street lamps and your flashlight at night, and under every unit. Turn off on slow machines."
+  STR_FPS_FLASHLIGHT: "Flashlight"
+  STR_FPS_FLASHLIGHT_DESC: "In the dark, the soldier's personal light (on/off with the game's personal light key) becomes a shoulder flashlight that lights where you look."
+  STR_FPS_COMBAT_MUSIC: "Combat music"
+  STR_FPS_COMBAT_MUSIC_DESC: "While aliens are in sight the music switches to a tenser track (base defence); it goes back to the battle music once they have been out of sight for a few seconds."
+  STR_FPS_LAUNCH_HINT: "Place the missile's waypoints, then press the launch button"
+  STR_FPS_FLARES: "Unlimited tactical flares"
+  STR_FPS_FLARES_DESC: "Throw a red flare (key T) at the crosshair; it bounces off walls, burns with red fire and red light for a minute. Under the sea it only goes a metre or two and bubbles hard. It lights the 3D view only: what the soldiers can see by the game's rules doesn't change."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_FLARE: "Throw flare"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_FLARE_DESC: "Throws a tactical flare at the crosshair (needs the tactical flares setting)."
+  STR_FPS_PSI_HINT: "Pick the creature on the map"
+  STR_FPS_VIEW_MODEL: "Weapon in hand"
+  STR_FPS_VIEW_MODEL_DESC: "Shows the weapon in the soldier's hand at the bottom right: it bobs as you walk, kicks when you fire and dips out of sight while reloading."
+  STR_FPS_VOXEL_WEAPON: "3D weapons (voxel)"
+  STR_FPS_VOXEL_WEAPON_DESC: "The weapon in hand gets volume: its inventory picture made of little cubes, each pixel as deep as its distance from the outline allows. NO: the flat picture on a plate."
+  STR_FPS_SPRITE_UPSCALE: "Sprite upscaling"
+  STR_FPS_SPRITE_UPSCALE_DESC: "Soldiers, aliens, items on the floor, explosions and smoke seen up close are scaled up the way pixel art scales well (xBRZ, in the game's own colours): Smooth rounds the stair-stepped edges, Smooth + detail also sharpens the shading a little. Off: the original pixels."
+  STR_FPS_UPSCALE_OFF: "Off"
+  STR_FPS_UPSCALE_SMOOTH: "Smooth"
+  STR_FPS_UPSCALE_DETAIL: "Smooth + detail"
+  STR_FPS_FAITHFUL_TARGETING: "Faithful X-COM targeting"
+  STR_FPS_DUAL_WIELD: "Dual wield"
+  STR_FPS_DUAL_WIELD_DESC: "YES: a soldier with a gun in each hand fires both at the same moment, round for round (each with its own fire mode, time units and ammo; in a burst the other gun's rounds go with the first ones), but each is half as accurate (in FPS-style shooting: twice the spread). Without the time units for both, only the chosen hand fires, at full accuracy. The 3D view shows the second gun on the other side. Two-handed weapons also take the game's own one-handed penalty. NO: one hand at a time, as in the game (G switches hands)."
+  STR_FPS_FAITHFUL_TARGETING_DESC: "YES: every shot uses the game's own accuracy (the hit chance by the crosshair). NO: FPS-style shooting: rounds fly along the crosshair with a spread (skill and kneeling tighten it; the dotted ring shows it) and recoil lifts your aim with every round. The game's three modes become: quick = BURST (one 3-round burst; guns without auto keep a quick single shot), AIMED = one tight round, AUTO = hold the trigger to keep firing until you let go or the clip is empty. Time units and damage are the game's."
+  STR_FPS_HOLD: "(HOLD)"
+  STR_FPS_MODE_BURST: "BURST"
+  STR_FPS_DUAL: "DUAL"
+  STR_FPS_FALLING: "Falling"
+  STR_FPS_FALLING_DESC: "YES: you can walk off a ledge and fall to the level below, hurt by the height (a little from one level, a lot from two or more; armor takes some). NO: ledges stop you, as on the map's paths."
+  STR_FPS_EYE_LOWER: "Eye height lowered by"
+  STR_FPS_EYE_LOWER_DESC: "X-COM soldiers fill a level almost to the ceiling; the 3D camera sits this many voxels lower (about 8 cm each) so rooms feel less cramped. 0 = the game's own eye height. The game's line of sight is not changed."
+  STR_FPS_MUZZLE_FLASH: "Muzzle flashes"
+  STR_FPS_MUZZLE_FLASH_DESC: "Gunfire lights up its surroundings for a blink and units flash when hit. Turn this off if flashing light bothers you (photosensitivity, epilepsy)."
+  STR_FPS_FLIGHT_COST: "Flight cost per level (TU)"
+  STR_FPS_FLIGHT_COST_DESC: "Time units a flying (or swimming) soldier pays to rise or sink one level with FLY switched on in 3D. 0 = free. The original game charges about 8."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_FLIGHT: "Flight on/off"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_FLIGHT_DESC: "Switches a flying armor's flight on and off. On: rise and sink with the up/down keys and move at that height. Off: you keep to the ground and won't step off ledges (an airborne soldier lands)."
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_FLY: "SUIT FLY"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_SWIM: "SUIT SWIM"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_LIGHT: "SUIT LIGHT"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_SPECIAL: "SPECIAL"
+  STR_FPS_NO_ARMOR: "No armor"
+  STR_FPS_FLIGHT_ON: "Flight on"
+  STR_FPS_FLIGHT_OFF: "Flight off"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_FLY_SHORT: "FLY"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_SWIM_SHORT: "SWIM"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_LIGHT_SHORT: "LIGHT"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_SPECIAL_SHORT: "SPEC"
+  STR_FPS_DECEASED: "DECEASED"
+  STR_FPS_UNCONSCIOUS: "UNCONSCIOUS"
+  STR_FPS_MIND_CONTROLLED: "MIND CONTROLLED"
+  STR_FPS_PANIC: "PANIC"
+  STR_FPS_BERSERK: "BERSERK"
+  STR_FPS_BURNING: "BURNING"
+  STR_FPS_ZOMBIE: "ZOMBIE"
+  STR_FPS_SIGNAL_LOST: "SIGNAL LOST"
+  STR_FPS_VAULT: "Jump over low obstacles"
+  STR_FPS_VAULT_DESC: "Jumping (Space) while walking into something low (a fence, a table, a crate, a rock: up to waist height) takes the soldier over it. The jump itself is free: only the walk to the far side costs its normal time units. NO: jumping is just a hop and the original rules decide what blocks you."
+  STR_FPS_NIGHT_VISION_GEAR: "Night vision needs gear"
+  STR_FPS_NIGHT_VISION_GEAR_DESC: "YES: in 3D only soldiers wearing or carrying night vision gear (power and flying suits, ion armor, hover tanks...; listed in the mod) and units that see in the dark, like aliens, get the NIGHT VISION button. NO: everyone has it, like on the isometric map."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_JUMP: "Jump"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_JUMP_DESC: "A free hop. Walking into a low obstacle, it vaults over it (see Jump over low obstacles). In 3D this key doesn't hold night vision (that's the night vision key)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NIGHT_VISION: "Night vision on/off"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NIGHT_VISION_DESC: "Switches night vision on and off in 3D, for a soldier with night vision gear (the NIGHT VISION button does the same)."
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_NIGHT: "NIGHT VISION"
+  STR_FPS_BUTTON_NIGHT_SHORT: "NV"
+  STR_FPS_NO_NIGHT_VISION: "No night vision gear"
+  STR_FPS_KILLED: "KILLED IN ACTION"
+  STR_FPS_ALL_LOST: "ALL SOLDIERS LOST"
+  STR_FPS_BREAKDOWN: "YOU HAVE A MENTAL BREAKDOWN"
+  STR_FPS_ZOMBIFIED: "TURNED INTO A ZOMBIE"
+  STR_FPS_LIFT: "LIFT PLATFORM"
+  STR_FPS_GAME_KEYS: "GAME KEYS THAT WORK IN 3D (ALSO IN CONTROLS)"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_TURN_LEFT: "Turn left"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_TURN_LEFT_DESC: "Turns the view left (the map's scroll left key)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_TURN_RIGHT: "Turn right"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_TURN_RIGHT_DESC: "Turns the view right (the map's scroll right key)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LOOK_UP: "Look up"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LOOK_UP_DESC: "Tilts the view up (the map's scroll up key)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LOOK_DOWN: "Look down"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LOOK_DOWN_DESC: "Tilts the view down (the map's scroll down key)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_ENEMY: "Turn to enemy {0}"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_ENEMY_DESC: "Turns the view to that visible enemy (the red buttons; the map's centre on enemy keys)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_KNEEL: "Kneel / stand"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_KNEEL_DESC: "Kneels or stands up, for the normal time units."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_INVENTORY: "Inventory"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_INVENTORY_DESC: "Opens the soldier's inventory (the INV button)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_RELOAD: "Reload"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_RELOAD_DESC: "Reloads the weapon in hand, for the normal time units."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LEFT_HAND: "Use left hand"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LEFT_HAND_DESC: "Opens the action menu of the item in the left hand."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_RIGHT_HAND: "Use right hand"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_RIGHT_HAND_DESC: "Opens the action menu of the item in the right hand."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LIGHT: "Personal light"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_LIGHT_DESC: "Personal light on/off (SUIT LIGHT); in the dark it's a shoulder flashlight."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NV_TOGGLE: "Night vision (map key)"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NV_TOGGLE_DESC: "The game's own night vision toggle. It works in 3D too, with night vision gear."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NEXT_UNIT: "Next soldier"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NEXT_UNIT_DESC: "Selects the next soldier who can still act (the > button)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_PREV_UNIT: "Previous soldier"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_PREV_UNIT_DESC: "Selects the previous soldier (the < button)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_END_TURN: "End turn"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_END_TURN_DESC: "Ends your turn (the END button)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_COUNTER: "Frame counter"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_COUNTER_DESC: "Shows frames per second in the top left corner."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_QUICK_SAVE: "Quick save"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_QUICK_SAVE_DESC: "Saves the battle to the quick save slot."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_QUICK_LOAD: "Quick load"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_QUICK_LOAD_DESC: "Loads the quick save."
+  STR_FPS_FRAME_LIMIT: "Frame rate limit"
+  STR_FPS_FRAME_LIMIT_DESC: "The game's frame rate cap (the same as in Advanced options). 60 is steady on modest machines at 1280x800; raise it for a 120 or 144 Hz screen if your computer keeps up (the frame counter shows it)."
+  STR_FPS_UNLIMITED: "Unlimited"
+  STR_FPS_FRAME_COUNTER: "Frame counter"
+  STR_FPS_FRAME_COUNTER_DESC: "Show frames per second in the top left corner (the same as F7)."
+  STR_FPS_CROSSHAIR: "Crosshair"
+  STR_FPS_CROSSHAIR_DESC: "Show the crosshair. Its shape shows the fire mode: open cross = snap, scope ring = aimed, brackets with one dot per round = auto, arc = throw, diamond = launcher, claws = melee, rings = psi."
+  STR_FPS_CROSSHAIR_INFO: "Shot info"
+  STR_FPS_CROSSHAIR_INFO_DESC: "Show the fire mode, hit chance and time unit cost under the crosshair. Yellow: you can, red: you can't (no time units, ammo or range)."
+  STR_FPS_AIM_EXACT: "Aim at exact point"
+  STR_FPS_AIM_EXACT_DESC: "YES: shots go for the exact point under the crosshair. NO: like the original game, shots go for the tile and the game picks the spot (the unit's centre, the object, the wall...). Accuracy applies either way."
+  STR_FPS_ALIEN_TURN_3D: "Alien turn in 3D"
+  STR_FPS_ALIEN_TURN_3D_DESC: "Stay in the 3D view during the alien turn, looking through your last soldier's eyes. NO switches back to the isometric map."
+  STR_FPS_START_IN_FIRST_PERSON: "Start battles in 3D"
+  STR_FPS_START_IN_FIRST_PERSON_DESC: "Begin each battle in the first-person view instead of the isometric map."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_TOGGLE_VIEW: "Isometric / 3D view"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_TOGGLE_VIEW_DESC: "Switches between the isometric map and the first-person view. Click a key, then press the new one; right click clears it."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MOUSE_MODE: "Mouse look / free cursor"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MOUSE_MODE_DESC: "In 3D the mouse turns the view; this key frees the cursor to click buttons (the middle mouse button does the same)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_FORWARD: "Walk forward"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_FORWARD_DESC: "Walk where you look. Crossing into the next tile costs its normal time units; walls and missing time units stop you."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_BACK: "Walk back"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_BACK_DESC: "Walk backwards."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_STRAFE_LEFT: "Step left"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_STRAFE_LEFT_DESC: "Walk sideways to the left."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_STRAFE_RIGHT: "Step right"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_STRAFE_RIGHT_DESC: "Walk sideways to the right."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NEXT_MODE: "Next fire mode"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_NEXT_MODE_DESC: "Cycles through what the left mouse button does with the weapon in hand (the mouse wheel does the same)."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MODE_SNAP: "Snap shot"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MODE_SNAP_DESC: "Picks the snap shot of the weapon in hand."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MODE_AIMED: "Aimed shot"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MODE_AIMED_DESC: "Picks the aimed shot of the weapon in hand."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MODE_AUTO: "Auto shot"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_MODE_AUTO_DESC: "Picks the auto shot (burst) of the weapon in hand."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_SWITCH_HAND: "Switch hand"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_SWITCH_HAND_DESC: "Uses the item in the other hand."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_UP: "Fly / lift up"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_UP_DESC: "Moves up a level with flying armour or on a gravity lift."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_DOWN: "Fly / lift down"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_DOWN_DESC: "Moves down a level with flying armour or on a gravity lift."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_DOOM_MODE: "Doom mode on/off"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_DOOM_MODE_DESC: "Toggles the debug cheat: endless time units, energy and ammo for the selected soldier."
+  STR_FPS_KEY_CLASSIC_HUD: "Classic HUD on/off"
+  STR_FPS_KEY_CLASSIC_HUD_DESC: "Shows the original bottom panel over the 3D view, e.g. to pick fire modes; the cursor is freed while it's shown."
